    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Let $ M_{1} $ and $ M_{2} $ denote the alternative sire alleles at a heterozygous marker locus, and let $ z_{ij} $ denote the phenotype of the jth individual with sire marker allele i. The simplest linear model for examining whether this marker is linked to a QTL (heterozygous in the sire) is",
      "source_page": 510,
