    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the marker effect $ m_{i} $ is the expected deviation from the mean trait value $ \\mu $, given that an offspring has sire allele $ M_{i} $. Since there are only two marker classes, a t test can be used to determine if offspring with $ M_{1} $ vs. $ M_{2} $ sire alleles have significantly different means,",
      "source_page": 510,
      "printed_page": 490,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p006:b8"
